## UI, access, and quality standards

- Reuse components from `frontend/lib/shared/` before creating module-specific UI; prioritize reusability and consistency.
- Responsive layouts for mobile, tablet, and desktop; keep UI uniform, simple, and intuitive.
- High performance worklists (pagination/lazy lists); localize all labels; no raw enum codes in production UI.
- Theme tokens only (`frontend/.cursor/design-system.mdc`); no hard-coded style values.
- Strict RBAC+ABAC: actions visible only when stage AND role AND subscription entitlement allow; hide unauthorized menus/components/workflows.
- Mutations: optimistic Riverpod update on HTTP success; WebSocket reconciliation (`.cursor/api-contract.mdc`).
- Reference entities by `human_friendly_id` / display IDs in UI and deep links — never raw table IDs.

